# OPTIONAL — tightly scoped NOPASSWD grant for the Raphael supervisor.
#
# WHY: config.yaml `paths.wsl_sudo: true` makes the supervisor run
# `sudo -n systemctl <verb> raphael-brain` over wsl.exe. There is no TTY for
# a password prompt, so without this grant every systemctl action fails with
# "interactive authentication required" (the supervisor logs a hint exactly
# about this). SKIP this file entirely if you run the default process mode
# (brain_mode: auto with the unit never installed) — process mode is
# root-less and needs no sudo at all.
#
# SCOPE: exactly three verbs on exactly ONE unit. Not a general systemctl
# grant, not a shell grant, no `!`-commands, no aliases.
#
# INSTALL (USER-run, needs sudo — agents never run this, AGENT_RULES §12):
#   scripts/install-brain-unit.sh --sudoers      (substitutes YOUR user and
#     the real systemctl path, then `visudo -cf` validates before install), or
#   manually: replace <USER> and /usr/bin/systemctl below, then
#     sudo visudo -f /etc/sudoers.d/raphael-brain   (editor — validates syntax)
#
# REMOVE:  sudo rm /etc/sudoers.d/raphael-brain
#
# Note: `systemctl is-active` / `show` are used unprivileged by the
# supervisor and need NO sudo entry. Ollama is intentionally absent here —
# profile cloud_temp never touches it (WAVES.md).
<USER> ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl start raphael-brain, /usr/bin/systemctl stop raphael-brain, /usr/bin/systemctl restart raphael-brain
